3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-18_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-19_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-20_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-21_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="3531e561-a5ff-42d3-a68c-915262af53f4" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How long is each recorded video?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-23_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-24_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-25_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-19160e9c-04b5-491d-bbf0-48d18e7b8d70"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">The dash cam uses loop recording. Each video clip can be set to <strong>1, 3, or 5 minutes </strong>in the settings.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-28_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-29_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="32fe95ec-89e1-40c3-9fa6-704b5ded754e" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Does the dash cam record sound?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-31_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-32_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-33_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-89e150c3-9fa6-404b-9ded-754eec68a319"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Yes, audio recording is enabled by default and can be turned off in the app settings.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-36_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-37_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="ffa2d3a6-8c91-4262-af53-f4df550b8ce1" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> What is loop recording and how does it work?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-39_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-40_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-41_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-9c04b569-1d3b-4048-918e-7b8d70579882"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> Loop recording automatically overwrites the oldest normal videos when the memory card is full. Emergency locked videos will not be overwritten.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-44_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-45_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="0b8ce14b-1916-4e9c-84b5-691d3bf048d1" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why can I only select 1/3/5 minutes? Can it record continuously?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-47_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-48_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-49_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-691d3bf0-48d1-4e7b-8d70-579882f16aca"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Short video segments ensure file safety and reliable playback. Continuous single-file recording is not recommended for dash cams.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-52_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-53_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="89e1f1ca-124f-4c22-9142-ed811f650f81" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> Parking Mode & G-Sensor</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-55_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-56_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-57_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-58_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-59_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="8c221142-ed81-4f65-8f81-870fabb95863" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What is Parking Mode and how does it work?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-61_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-62_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-63_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-ed811f65-0f81-470f-abb9-5863dcb97b4b"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> Parking Mode requires a dedicated hardwire kit. When the car is parked, the dash cam will automatically record and lock videos if a collision is detected.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-66_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-67_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="0f81870f-abb9-4863-9cb9-7b4b26dcc6d3" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How do I turn on Parking Monitor?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-69_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-70_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-71_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-abb95863-dcb9-4b4b-a6dc-c6d3921d7015"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> Install the hardwire kit first, then enable Parking Mode or Collision Detection in the app settings.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-74_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-75_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="dcb97b4b-26dc-46d3-921d-7015a9efb0f6" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How long can Parking Mode work without starting the car?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-77_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-78_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-79_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-26dcc6d3-921d-4015-a9ef-b0f68cb7efd2"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> It depends on your car battery capacity. The hardwire kit has low-voltage protection and will cut off power automatically to protect the battery.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-82_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-83_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="921d7015-a9ef-40f6-8cb7-efd27bee35d0" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What is the G-sensor used for?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-85_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-86_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-87_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-a9efb0f6-8cb7-4fd2-bbee-35d06b585f14"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">The built-in G-sensor detects impacts or sudden vibrations and automatically locks the current video to prevent overwriting.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-90_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-91_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="13faccff-693b-43a6-9584-b411ce0f22ed" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why doesn’t the G-sensor trigger when I tap the car by hand?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-93_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-94_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-95_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-693b83a6-5584-4411-8e0f-22ed2a00467c"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Hand tapping is usually not strong enough. The G-sensor is designed to respond to real collisions or significant vibrations.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-98_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-99_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="992c4d65-205e-4700-8af5-9d81d77d2030" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Memory Card & Storage</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-101_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-102_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-103_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-104_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-105_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="9ce23df1-4af8-4992-a89b-c0e1eda1acd1" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What memory card should I use?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-107_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-108_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-109_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-9f7be3b8-5867-4c66-ab9c-85d7cd170a24"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">We recommend a branded micro SD card, Class 10 / U3, 64GB–256GB. Please format the card regularly.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-112_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-113_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="f8c99268-9bc0-41ed-a1ac-d188ef2bad85" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Do I need to delete files manually?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-115_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-116_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-117_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-b858672c-66ab-4c85-97cd-170a245a9bfe"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> No. Normal videos are automatically overwritten. Only locked videos need manual deletion if storage is full.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-120_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-121_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="3886a18f-9eaa-425e-bb12-ce453847b206" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>WiFi,  App & Playback</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-123_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-124_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-125_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-126_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-127_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="cf6cfd21-d6cb-4579-9a96-42439ecb62a5" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why does it say “No Internet Connection” after connecting WiFi?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-129_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-130_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-131_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-62a5f816-5767-4ff0-aa79-18482f528abc"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">This is a local WiFi connection prompt. The dashcam's WiFi does not provide internet access; it is solely for establishing a connection. This message is normal.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-134_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-135_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="cb25791a-9642-439e-8b62-a5f8165767ef" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Can I view videos remotely?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-137_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-138_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-139_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-165767ef-f06a-4918-882f-528abcabfed7"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> No. Remote viewing is not supported. Videos can be viewed via WiFi when you are near the vehicle.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-142_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-143_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="42439ecb-62a5-4816-9767-eff06a791848" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Can I view videos on my PC?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-145_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-146_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-147_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-eff06a79-1848-4f52-8abc-abfed7ef902e"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Yes. Remove the SD card and use a card reader or connect it to your computer.<br></span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-150_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-151_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="ce453847-b206-40bc-8063-0fdc0884cdfb" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Installation & Others</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-153_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-154_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-155_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-156_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-157_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="a6704b5d-ed75-4eec-a8a3-19caecbc6a63" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> Is it normal for the dash cam to get warm?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-159_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-160_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-161_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-6a637b54-1490-47c0-873e-51dde9f14438"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Yes. Heat during 4K recording or WiFi use is normal and within safe operating limits.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-164_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-165_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="e9f14438-374f-441b-a674-c3e61b7d9c2e" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Can I power the dash cam with a power bank?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-167_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-168_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-169_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-374fe41b-a674-43e6-9b7d-9c2e99bad9d7"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Not recommended. A power bank may cause unstable voltage and abnormal operation.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-172_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-173_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="99bad9d7-5dce-4711-be45-3904ff7ccab1" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How long is the warranty?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-175_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-176_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-177_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-5dce2711-3e45-4904-bf7c-cab17851a7bb"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">The standard warranty is<strong> 1 year</strong>, and we also provide<strong> lifetime technical support</strong>. If you <strong>register your product</strong>, you can <strong>extend the warranty by 1 additional year</strong> (for a total of<strong> 2 years</strong>).</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-180_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-181_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="fc2af001-44a7-4309-9964-f4833c175e33" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How to use the static cling sticker?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-183_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-184_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-185_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-44a7e309-d964-4483-bc17-5e33a1596611"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">First clean the glass → Apply the static cling sticker → Then attach the 3M mount to the static cling sticker for easy removal later.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-188_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-189_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="a814d604-6e16-4639-9edf-bdb3dad24225" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How to remove 3M adhesive?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-191_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-192_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-193_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-6e168639-1edf-4db3-9ad2-42259439106e"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Use a hairdryer to heat the adhesive, then slowly peel it off. This method won't damage the glass.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-196_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-197_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="e680a544-76b6-43b0-94a7-08d984afc38d" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How long is the rear camera cable?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-199_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-200_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-201_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-76b663b0-54a7-48d9-84af-c38d77a32194"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">The rear camera cable is<strong> 19.69 ft</strong> long. If the cable isn’t long enough for your vehicle, we also offer a <strong>rear camera extension cable</strong>. Please contact the <strong>GKU support team</strong>, and they can send you one.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-204_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-205_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="d32191d1-1104-48fd-8b7f-7b3531e561a5" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Troubleshooting</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-207_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-208_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-209_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-210_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-211_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="f9a090ab-62ca-4198-ab46-17c8970dccf8" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Time & Recording Issues</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-213_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-214_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-215_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-216_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-217_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="4107289e-0840-457e-a94d-e09bb0de4072" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The recorded video time does not match the system time. What should I do?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-219_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-220_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-221_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-7bdaeaad-45bd-46f4-8dea-13d5fd87065f"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> Connect the dash cam to the app via WiFi and confirm time sync. Check your phone’s time/time zone. Try a factory reset. If it persists, contact support.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-224_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-225_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="4635c51d-59e8-4ab0-bd88-d87f8afc6440" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Overheating</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-227_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-228_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-229_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-230_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-231_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="aab03d88-d87f-4afc-a440-b2df732629ac" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why does the dash cam get hot during use?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-233_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-234_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-235_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-d87f8afc-6440-42df-b326-29ac4131f09f"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Mild heat is normal, especially during 4K recording, parking mode, or direct sunlight. The operating range is -4°F to 158°F. If it overheats abnormally, shuts down, or shows a high-temp warning, contact support.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-238_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-239_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="e6bb2b76-e6cf-47f3-98bf-73c20319d911" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Playback Issues</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-241_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-242_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-243_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-244_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-245_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="d7f358bf-73c2-4319-9911-faccb54c5fef" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Video playback is choppy or freezes. What should I do?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-247_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-248_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-249_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-73c20319-d911-4acc-b54c-5fef2ab56598"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">In the app, download the video first, then play. On PC, use recommended players like PotPlayer or GKU Player. If it continues, provide an SD card photo to support.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-252_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-253_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="f8e5d92e-c7b6-49cf-998c-c673f4c9844e" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Power & Recording Problems</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-255_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-256_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-257_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-258_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-259_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="99cf598c-c673-44c9-844e-f07b23302d81" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The dash cam beeps after power-on and does not record.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-261_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-262_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-263_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-c673f4c9-844e-407b-a330-2d8197301858"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Check the power supply. Test at home using USB-A to USB-C power. Try a different SD card. If it persists, contact support.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-266_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-267_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="97301858-fc18-4ada-9888-adbb68c928e4" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The dash cam doesn’t record continuously or some videos are missing.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-269_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-270_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-271_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-fc186ada-5888-4dbb-a8c9-28e43a9aa642"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Ensure stable power. Check both the loop folder and the locked folder. Test at home recording for 1–2 hours with a phone USB charger, then verify in the app. If it persists, contact support.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-274_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-275_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="27584adb-03f3-4ecc-9f82-3b615559ea25" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>G-Sensor & Voice Alerts</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-277_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-278_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-279_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-280_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-281_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="4ecc9f82-3b61-4559-aa25-5e81bbbc84b2" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why does the dash cam frequently announce “Video Locked”?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-283_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-284_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-285_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-3b615559-ea25-4e81-bbbc-84b26931f182"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Connect to WiFi and lower the G-sensor sensitivity if it’s too high. If it persists, contact support and provide the firmware version.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-288_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-289_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="5d7de40d-065c-47a1-a74d-4946aa143877" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Power Issues</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-291_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-292_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-293_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-294_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-295_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="77a1a74d-4946-4a14-b877-9c874000c158" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The dash cam doesn’t turn on.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-297_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-298_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-299_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-4946aa14-3877-4c87-8000-c158b8b4dfa1"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Check the power cable and source. Test with a wall charger using USB-A to USB-C. Do not use USB-C to USB-C cable as it may cause compatibility issues. If it still won’t power on, contact support.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-302_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-303_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="1fbd3e3b-29cc-4303-8bbc-b7310b2187fb" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>WiFi Password & Settings</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-305_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-306_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-307_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-308_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-309_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="a3034bbc-b731-4b21-87fb-4663cf06d226" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What is the default WiFi password?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-311_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-312_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-313_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-b7310b21-87fb-4663-8f06-d226d7e2e72a"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">The default password is 12345678</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-316_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-317_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="d7e2e72a-1d1a-4b35-85bd-a0c5a0aaad3c" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>How do I change the WiFi password?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-319_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-320_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-321_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-1d1acb35-05bd-40c5-a0aa-ad3cbf409e94"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Reset the dash cam and connect using the default password. In the app go to Camera Settings → WiFi Password. After changing it, forget the old network on your phone and reconnect. Use numbers only.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-324_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-325_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="bf409e94-46c7-436d-8457-a765ec7dfaae" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why can’t I reconnect after changing the WiFi password?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-327_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-328_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-329_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-46c7936d-4457-4765-ac7d-faae89011428"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Forget the previous dash cam WiFi network in your phone settings and reconnect with the new password. Special characters are not supported.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-332_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-333_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="c7ee04c9-52a7-4ae7-b819-660868e8bedf" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Android-Specific</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-335_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-336_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-337_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-338_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-339_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="9ae7b819-6608-48e8-bedf-0bf2b3b2f2a5" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Android WiFi connection fails or disconnects automatically.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-341_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-342_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-343_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-660868e8-bedf-4bf2-b3b2-f2a5e46079ff"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">When prompted, select “Stay connected even without internet.” Also disable VPN and nearby car WiFi systems (CarPlay/Android Auto) that may interfere.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-346_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-347_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="bedf0bf2-b3b2-42a5-a460-79ff3d939c39" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Android has no internet after connecting to the dash cam WiFi.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-349_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-350_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-351_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-b3b2f2a5-e460-49ff-bd93-9c390cd2b184"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">This is normal due to Android system behavior. Disconnect from the dash cam WiFi when you need internet. Recording is not affected.</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-354_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-355_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="13fbcbe2-6c70-4666-9b00-e2387099b988" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> Memory Card (SD Card)</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-357_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-358_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-359_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-360_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-361_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="f666db00-e238-4099-b988-af2d3f354dff" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> It says “Please format the memory card” / “Card error”. What should I do?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-363_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-364_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-365_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-e2387099-b988-4f2d-bf35-4dff27eaa7fa"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">  Step-by-step:<br> <br>1) Power on the dash cam and connect your phone to the dash cam WiFi<br><br>2) Open the APP → Settings → Format SD Card<br> <br>3) After formatting, record for 5–10 minutes and check whether new files are created<br> <br>4) If the message returns, remove the card and do a slow format on a computer with a card reader (do not quick format)<br> <br>5) Insert the card back into the dash cam, then format again inside the APP</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-368_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-369_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="b988af2d-3f35-4dff-a7ea-a7fabf48fb8f" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> The dash cam beeps after power-on and doesn’t record.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-371_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-372_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-373_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-3f354dff-27ea-47fa-bf48-fb8f4dfb31c9"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br> <br>1) Confirm stable power supply (use the original car charger)<br><br>2) Test the camera at home with a wall charger using USB-A to USB-C<br> <br>3) Replace the memory card and test again<br> <br>4) If it still doesn’t record, format the card in the APP once more</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-376_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-377_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="5bcbaeaf-1407-407c-ae21-6f0c3dd03687" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Some videos are missing / it’s not recording in a loop.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-379_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-380_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-381_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-1407e07c-6e21-4f0c-bdd0-368778d2982e"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) Confirm Loop Recording is enabled in settings<br><br>2) Check both folders: - Loop/Normal folder (regular recording) - Locked/Emergency folder (protected clips)<br><br>3) Test recording at home for 1–2 hours with a stable wall charger<br> <br>4) If the locked folder is full (G-sensor too sensitive), lower the G-sensor sensitivity<br> <br>5) If the SD card is near full and loop doesn’t work, back up files and format the card</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-384_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-385_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="0b6d5cb9-b41c-49e2-9854-8bb03da61e8f" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Video playback fails on PC or shows “playback error”.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-387_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-388_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-389_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-b41ca9e2-5854-4bb0-bda6-1e8f5e782970"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) Remove the SD card and use a card reader to play the files on a computer <br><br>2) If the files are in TS format, use PotPlayer (or GKU Player) to open them<br> <br>3) If videos play fine on PC, the camera is recording normally and the issue is likely the APP/WiFi connection <br><br>4) If videos also fail on PC, the files may be corrupted — format the card and test again</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-392_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-393_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="a3cefca6-bcc4-4152-b996-f65d6114b8fd" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> I use 256GB/512GB and it freezes or becomes unstable.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-395_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-396_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-397_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-bcc4e152-b996-465d-a114-b8fdaab81425"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) Do a slow format on PC (not quick format)<br> <br>2) Insert into the dash cam and format again in the APP <br><br>3) Use a high-quality card (example: SanDisk Extreme microSD)<br><br>4) If the issue continues, switch to 128GB for best stability</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-400_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-401_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="f9dc2c8d-a90b-4180-9dd1-4b04e47bcb70" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>APP & WiFi</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-403_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-404_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-405_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-406_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-407_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="01801dd1-4b04-447b-8b70-63e0f48963ab" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>I connected to WiFi, but it says “No Internet” / “WiFi has no internet access”.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-409_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-410_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-411_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-4b04e47b-cb70-43e0-b489-63ab65769522"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) This is normal: dash cam WiFi is a hub-type WiFi for data transfer only<br> <br>2) Keep your phone within 3–5 meters<br> <br>3) Open the APP and add/connect the camera normally</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-414_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-415_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="cb7063e0-f489-43ab-a576-9522b3aaac45" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>I can’t connect to the dash cam WiFi.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-417_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-418_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-419_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-f48963ab-6576-4522-b3aa-ac454187d061"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br> <br>1) Confirm the dash cam is powered on and recording (indicator light blinking)<br> <br>2) Stand within 3–5 meters<br> <br>3) Turn off: VPN, Bluetooth, mobile data, security/antivirus apps<br> <br>4) On your phone WiFi list, tap the device WiFi and select Forget This Network<br> <br>5) Factory reset the camera (press/hold the function button for &gt;5 seconds)<br> <br>6) Reconnect to device WiFi and enter the default password 12345678 <br><br>7) Open the APP and add the camera</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-422_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-423_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="65769522-b3aa-4c45-8187-d06185f190e9" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The dash cam WiFi name doesn’t show up (can’t find WiFi).</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-425_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-426_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-427_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-b3aaac45-4187-4061-85f1-90e9b14e2323"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) Use the original car charger and start the engine to ensure full power<br><br>2) If still not found, do a factory reset (hold the function button &gt;5 seconds)<br> <br>3) Test at home with a wall charger and USB-A to USB-C cable (stable power)<br> <br>4) If it works at home, the vehicle power supply may be unstable</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-430_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-431_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="4187d061-85f1-40e9-b14e-23235a5f58bf" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>The APP can’t preview / buffering is slow / can’t download videos.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-433_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-434_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-435_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-85f190e9-b14e-4323-9a5f-58bf3bb93a12"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br><br>1) Keep the phone close (within 3–5m) and ensure WiFi is stable<br><br>2) Turn off mobile data while connected to the dash cam WiFi<br> <br>3) For 4K files, download first, then play from your phone gallery to avoid buffering<br> <br>4) If preview/download still fails: - Delete the APP and reinstall the latest version - Test the SD card on a PC via card reader to confirm the files are OK</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-438_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-439_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="b14e2323-5a5f-48bf-bbb9-3a12e5a7702e" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why can’t I see videos in the APP “Album”?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-441_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-442_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-443_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-5a5f58bf-3bb9-4a12-a5a7-702e88710a5b"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step:<br> <br>1) The “Album” shows only the files you downloaded to the phone<br><br>2) Connect to dash cam WiFi → open playback → select videos → download<br> <br>3) After download, they will appear in the APP Album / phone gallery</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-446_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-447_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="cb15f2d7-5722-408a-814c-2f2492cece6d" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Parking Monitor</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-449_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-450_"><div class="sc-gvZzpm gKmDqk pf-451_ pf-icon-right" data-scroll-to-top="true" data-open-multiple="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3"><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-452_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-453_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="f08ac14c-2f24-42ce-8e6d-e4f3d8dc69e0" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span> How do I install the hardwire kit (step-down voltage kit)?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-455_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-456_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-457_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-2f2492ce-ce6d-44f3-98dc-69e0cbb7bf56"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "><strong>Step 1: Locate your vehicle’s fuse box</strong><br>Please find your fuse box using your vehicle’s Fuse Box Diagram (owner’s manual or fuse box cover diagram). Please open the fuse box cover. Some covers lift by a small tab; others may require gently prying a panel—please use the included trim tool if needed.<br><br>If you have trouble locating the fuse box, please let us know and we’ll help.<br><br><strong>Step 2: Identify the correct fuse slots (ACC + Constant Power)</strong><br>You will need two fuse slots:<br><br>Constant Power fuse (Yellow wire): provides power all the time, even when the engine is off. (Required for parking mode.)<br><br>ACC fuse (Red wire): provides power only when the key is in ACC/ON. (Used for normal driving recording.)<br><br><strong>Step 3: Connect the Red &amp; Yellow fuse taps (Add-A-Fuse) and verify with a voltmeter</strong><br>Please use a voltmeter to confirm you picked the correct fuse slots:<br><br>Red Wire (ACC): Please turn the car key to the ACC position.Please test the aluminum end of the RED Add-A-Fuse with a voltmeter.If you see voltage, it confirms this slot is powered in ACC.<br><br>Yellow Wire (Constant/B+): Please turn the car off. Please test the aluminum end of the YELLOW Add-A-Fuse with a voltmeter. If you still see voltage, it confirms this slot is constant (always-on) power.<br><br><strong>Step 4: Locate a good ground point (Black wire)<br></strong>Please connect the Black wire (Ground) to a solid metal screw/bolt on the vehicle chassis. We strongly recommend using a proper ground point for stable power.<br><br>Please note: an improper ground connection may cause the dash cam to malfunction or restart intermittently.<br><br>After wiring, please power on the dash cam and confirm it records normally.Please check that Parking Mode appears in the app/settings after a correct hardwire installation. If your fuse type doesn’t match the fuse taps you have, please contact us</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-460_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-461_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="ce6de4f3-d8dc-49e0-8bb7-bf566740d023" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Parking Monitoring option doesn’t appear in the APP.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-463_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-464_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-465_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-d8dc69e0-cbb7-4f56-a740-d0231353b77a"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step (<strong>wiring verification</strong>):<br> <br>1) Use a multimeter to find the correct fuses: - ACC fuse (for RED wire): - Engine ON: has power - Engine OFF: 0V - BATT/Constant fuse (for YELLOW wire): - Engine ON: has power - Engine OFF: 12V+ <br><br>2) Connect BLACK wire to a metal ground point <br><br>3) Restart the car, power on the dash cam, connect WiFi, and check the APP again <br><br>4) If Parking Monitoring still doesn’t show, re-check fuse selection and wiring</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-468_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-469_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="cbb7bf56-6740-4023-9353-b77ad08d6620" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>After the car is off, I can’t connect to the dash cam WiFi / the camera looks “offline”.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-471_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-472_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-473_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-6740d023-1353-477a-908d-662037ab1842"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step: <br><br>1) This can be normal in parking mode: WiFi may be disabled to reduce power and prevent tampering<br><br> 2) To check parking recordings: - Start the car → connect WiFi → open playback - Look for time-lapse files in the loop folder (often with “tlp” in the filename) - Look for collision-triggered files in the locked folder</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-476_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-477_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="1353b77a-d08d-4620-b7ab-1842cc5d6a8d" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Time-lapse parking videos play very fast. Is that normal?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-479_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-480_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-481_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-d08d6620-37ab-4842-8c5d-6a8dca1d5055"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step: <br><br>1) Yes. Time-lapse records at a very low frame rate (e.g., 1 frame per second) <br><br>2) That means a short clip may contain a long parking period, so playback looks fast <br><br>3) For better viewing, download the file and play on a PC with PotPlayer</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-484_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-485_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="37ab1842-cc5d-4a8d-8a1d-5055b1be116c" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Will parking mode drain my car battery?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-487_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-488_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-489_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-cc5d6a8d-ca1d-4055-b1be-116c1479b869"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> Step-by-step:<br><br>1) The hardwire kit has low-voltage protection and will cut off power when voltage drops below about 11.8V <br><br>2) Battery drain risk depends on your battery health and how long the car is parked <br><br>3) To reduce risk: - Use Collision Detection mode for long parking - Or set a limited time-lapse duration (e.g., 12h/24h) instead of always-on</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-492_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-493_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="1bd3c631-0524-4bae-8a8f-4ab51c405286" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>After installing the fuse tap, my car’s original function stopped working.</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-495_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-496_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-497_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-0524bbae-ca8f-4ab5-9c40-52864c5c8a54"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "> Step-by-step: <br><br>1) Make sure you inserted the original vehicle fuse back into the fuse tap<br><br>2) The fuse tap has two slots: one for the original circuit fuse, one for the dash cam <br><br>3) After installation, test both the vehicle function and dash cam power</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-kRRxPL iQTArD pf-500_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-kqGpvY cmTzNW pf-501_ pf-bg-lazy pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="fb564ae4-100b-470e-9260-826961d21153" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>What fuse rating can the hardwire kit use? Can it go into a 15A or higher slot?</span></div></summary><div class="sc-dxcExB boHSLB pf-503_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-ijaoyg fLgXwO pf-504_"><p class="sc-stwUW giqUXE pf-505_" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-100bd70e-5260-4269-a1d2-1153f0abe702"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Step-by-step: <br><br>1) The hardwire kit supports up to 15A <br><br>2) In parking mode, the dash cam current is typically under 700mA <br><br>3) You can use a 15A-or-higher fuse slot as long as that circuit is not shared with other high-load devices</span></p></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details></div></div></div></div></details></div></div></section></div></div></div><script>
